# The layers that deny the model's central claim, and the argument each one makes. One row per
# corpus layer filing the `absent` branch of `StatedRemainder`, beside how many corpus layers there
# are to deny it.
#
# It works as a pair with the independence report
#   This model makes two claims a document can refute in the model's own format, and each has a
#   wrapper built to carry the refusal. `Coupling` says the layers hold their remainders
#   independently, and the search beside it records whether anybody looked. `StatedRemainder` says
#   every layer has a remainder, and requiring the wrapper makes a sender who disagrees say so
#   explicitly rather than leave a field empty. The first has never been confirmed and has been
#   contradicted. This report is the second.
#
# The rows need the second branch
#   They can be seen only because `ingest.sql` reads the second branch. Read without it, a denial
#   arrives as five NULLs, with sign, absorber and quantity all blank, which is exactly the shape of
#   a document that said nothing. `refutation/object-storage` foresaw that in its own note: "filed
#   as a counter-example to the claim that every layer carries a remainder, not as a gap in this
#   document".
#
# Corpus only
#   On the same argument as the independence report. "The model has been contradicted" is a claim
#   about the evidence. A fixture that denies a remainder shows the branch works and says nothing
#   whatever about the world, so counting one here would make up a refutation nobody made.
-- pm:StatedRemainder's absent branch, over the corpus.
SELECT d.filing, d.layer, d.reason,
       regexp_replace(d.argument, '\s+', ' ', 'g') AS the_counter_example,
       format('%s of %s corpus layers deny having one',
              count(*) OVER (),
              (SELECT count(*) FROM (
                    :compose(layers/every_layer.sqlc)
                ) l
                JOIN (
                    :compose(scope/corpus.sqlc)
                ) sc USING (filing))) AS how_common
FROM (
    :compose(layers/denied_remainders.sqlc)
) d
JOIN (
    :compose(scope/corpus.sqlc)
) s USING (filing)
ORDER BY d.filing, d.layer
